{"slug": "base64-encode-decode", "title": "Base64 Encode / Decode", "h1": "Base64 Encode / Decode", "category": "other", "categoryTitle": "Other Calculators", "description": "This free online tool can Base64-encode or decode text, images, and files directly in the browser without sending the data across the internet.", "html": "<div id=\"breadcrumbs\" itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/BreadcrumbList\"><span itemprop=\"itemListElement\" itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/ListItem\"><a href=\"/index\" itemprop=\"item\"><span itemprop=\"name\">home</span></a><meta content=\"1\" itemprop=\"position\"/></span> / <span itemprop=\"itemListElement\" itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/ListItem\"><a href=\"/other-calculator\" itemprop=\"item\"><span itemprop=\"name\">other</span></a><meta content=\"2\" itemprop=\"position\"/></span> / <span itemprop=\"itemListElement\" itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/ListItem\"><a href=\"/base64-encode-decode\" itemprop=\"item\"><span itemprop=\"name\">base64 encode / decode</span></a><meta content=\"3\" itemprop=\"position\"/></span></div> <h1>Base64 Encode / Decode</h1>\n<p>Use the tools below to Base64-encode or decode text, images, and files. To ensure data safety, the encoding and decoding are performed within the browser without being sent across the internet.</p>\n<div class=\"panel\">\n<form name=\"calcexpress\">\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><div>Text to encode or decode:</div>\n<textarea class=\"infulltxarea\" name=\"cinput\" rows=\"3\"></textarea>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Character:\n\t\t\t<select class=\"inlongest\" name=\"cchar\">\n<option selected=\"\" value=\"utf-8\">UTF-8</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1252\">ASCII</option>\n<option value=\"utf-16le\">UTF-16</option>\n<option value=\"utf-16be\">UTF-16BE</option>\n<option value=\"big5\">Big5 (Chinese)</option>\n<option value=\"gb18030\">GB 18030 (Chinese)</option>\n<option value=\"gb2312\">GB 2312 (Chinese)</option>\n<option value=\"euc-jp\">EUC-JP (Japanese)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-2022-jp\">ISO-2022-JP (Japanese)</option>\n<option value=\"shift-jis\">Shift JIS (Japanese)</option>\n<option value=\"euc-kr\">EUC-KR (Korean)</option>\n<option value=\"ibm866\">CP866 (Russian)</option>\n<option value=\"koi8-r\">KOI8-R (Russian)</option>\n<option value=\"koi8-u\">KOI8-U (Ukrainian)</option>\n<option value=\"macintosh\">Macintosh (x-mac-roman)</option>\n<option value=\"x-mac-cyrillic\">Mac OS Cyrillic (x-mac-cyrillic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-1\">ISO-8859-1 (Latin1/Western European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-2\">ISO-8859-2 (Latin2/Eastern European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-3\">ISO-8859-3 (Latin3/South European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-4\">ISO-8859-4 (Latin4/North European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-5\">ISO-8859-5 (Latin/Cyrillic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-6\">ISO-8859-6 (Latin/Arabic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-7\">ISO-8859-7 (Latin/Greek)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-8\">ISO-8859-8 (Latin/Hebrew)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-8-i\">ISO-8859-8-I (Latin/Hebrew)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-10\">ISO-8859-10 (Latin6/Nordic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-13\">ISO-8859-13 (Latin7/Baltic Rim)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-14\">ISO-8859-14 (Latin8/Celtic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-15\">ISO-8859-15 (Latin9/Western European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-16\">ISO-8859-16 (Latin10/South-Eastern European)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-874\">Windows-874 (Thai)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1250\">Windows-1250 (Eastern European)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1251\">Windows-1251 (Cyrillic)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1252\">Windows-1252 (Western European)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1253\">Windows-1253 (Greek)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1254\">Windows-1254 (Turkish)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1255\">Windows-1255 (Hebrew)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1256\">Windows-1256 (Arabic)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1257\">Windows-1257 (Baltic)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1258\">Windows-1258 (Vietnamese)</option>\n</select>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 8px 0px;\">\n<input name=\"e\" onclick=\"return bcEncode();\" type=\"submit\" value=\" Encode\"/>\n<input name=\"d\" onclick=\"return bcDecode();\" type=\"submit\" value=\" Decode\"/>\n<input onclick=\"clearForm(document.calcexpress);\" type=\"button\" value=\"Clear\"/>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div id=\"coutputdesc\"></div>\n<div id=\"coutputarea\" style=\"display:none;\"><textarea class=\"infulltxarea\" name=\"coutput\" readonly=\"\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</form>\n</div>\n<script>\nfunction bcDownloadTxtFile(bcdObj, bcdFilename){\n\tlet bcdFileToUse = bcdFilename;\n\tif (bcdFilename.length<1) bcdFileToUse = \"base64-\"+(Date.now()%10000)+\".txt\";\n\tconst blob = new Blob([bcdObj.value]);\n\tconst url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n\tconst a = document.createElement('a');\n\ta.href = url;\n\ta.download = bcdFileToUse;\n\tdocument.body.appendChild(a);\n\ta.click();\n\tdocument.body.removeChild(a);\n\tURL.revokeObjectURL(url);\n\treturn false;\n}\nfunction bcInt8ArrToB64(bbBytes) {return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...bbBytes));}\nfunction bcEncode(){\n\tlet bceInTxt = document.calcexpress.cinput.value + \"\";\n\tlet bceOutputdesc = document.getElementById(\"coutputdesc\");\n\tif (bceInTxt.length < 1){\n\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Please enter text to encode.</font>';\n\t}else{\n\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = 'processing...';\n\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"coutputarea\").style.display = \"block\";\n\t\tlet bcEncoder = new TextEncoder();\n\t\t//document.calcexpress.coutput.value = bcEncoder.encode(bceInTxt).toBase64();\n\t\tdocument.calcexpress.coutput.value = bcInt8ArrToB64(bcEncoder.encode(bceInTxt));\n\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<b>Encoded result:</b> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcCopyOutput();\"><img src=\"img/copy.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"20\" alt=\"copy\" align=\"absmiddle\">copy</a> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcDownloadTxtFile(document.calcexpress.coutput, \\'\\');\"><img src=\"img/download.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"download\" align=\"absmiddle\">download</a>';\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\nfunction bcB64ToInt8Arr(bcB64) {\n\tconst bcBStr = window.atob(bcB64);\n\tconst bcBStrLen = bcBStr.length;\n\tconst bcOut = new Uint8Array(bcBStrLen);\n\tfor (let i = 0; i < bcBStrLen; i++) bcOut[i] = bcBStr.charCodeAt(i);\n\treturn bcOut;\n}\nfunction bcDecode(){\n\tlet bcdInTxt = document.calcexpress.cinput.value + \"\";\n\tlet bcdChar = document.calcexpress.cchar.value + \"\";\n\tlet bcdOutputdesc = document.getElementById(\"coutputdesc\");\n\ttry {\n\t\tif (bcdInTxt.length < 1){\n\t\t\tbcdOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Please enter text to decode.</font>';\n\t\t}else{\n\t\t\tbcdOutputdesc.innerHTML = 'processing...';\n\t\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"coutputarea\").style.display = \"block\";\n\t\t\tlet bcDecoder = new TextDecoder(bcdChar);\n\t\t\t//document.calcexpress.coutput.value = bcDecoder.decode(Uint8Array.fromBase64(bcdInTxt));\n\t\t\tdocument.calcexpress.coutput.value = bcDecoder.decode(bcB64ToInt8Arr(bcdInTxt));\n\t\t\tbcdOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<b>Decoded result:</b> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcCopyOutput();\"><img src=\"img/copy.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"20\" alt=\"copy\" align=\"absmiddle\">copy</a> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcDownloadTxtFile(document.calcexpress.coutput, \\'\\');\"><img src=\"img/download.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"download\" align=\"absmiddle\">download</a>';\n\t\t}\n\t} catch (err) {\n\t\tbcdOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Sorry, the input text cannot be Base64-decoded.</font>';\n\t\tdocument.calcexpress.coutput.value = \"\";\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\nfunction bcCopyOutput() {\n\tlet bcTxt = document.calcexpress.coutput.value + \"\";\n\ttry {\n\t\tnavigator.clipboard.writeText(bcTxt);\n\t} catch (err) {\n\t\tdocument.calcexpress.coutput.select();\n\t\tdocument.execCommand('copy');\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\n</script>\n<br/>\n<h2>Base64 Encode / Decode an Image or File</h2>\n<p>Use the tool below to Base64-encode or decode images and files. For text output, the result will be shown in the text area with options to copy or download. For image and binary output, the generated file will be downloaded directly. For large files, the encoding and decoding may take some time.</p>\n<div class=\"panel\">\n<form name=\"calcfull\">\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td>I want to:\n\t\t\t<select name=\"coptype\" onchange=\"cOpChange(this.value);\">\n<option selected=\"\" value=\"en\">encode a file</option>\n<option value=\"de\">decode a file</option>\n</select>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 8px 0px;\">\n<div><input class=\"infull\" id=\"cFileInput\" name=\"cFileInput\" type=\"file\"/></div>\n<div id=\"cdivfiletype\" style=\"display:none;\">Output file type:\n\t\t\t<select name=\"cfiletype\" onchange=\"cFileTypeChange(this.value);\">\n<option selected=\"\" value=\"txt\">Text file</option>\n<option value=\"img\">Binary or Image</option>\n</select></div>\n<div id=\"cdivchar\" style=\"padding-top: 8px;display:none;\">Character:\n\t\t\t<select class=\"inlongest\" name=\"cchar\">\n<option selected=\"\" value=\"utf-8\">UTF-8</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1252\">ASCII</option>\n<option value=\"utf-16le\">UTF-16</option>\n<option value=\"utf-16be\">UTF-16BE</option>\n<option value=\"big5\">Big5 (Chinese)</option>\n<option value=\"gb18030\">GB 18030 (Chinese)</option>\n<option value=\"gb2312\">GB 2312 (Chinese)</option>\n<option value=\"euc-jp\">EUC-JP (Japanese)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-2022-jp\">ISO-2022-JP (Japanese)</option>\n<option value=\"shift-jis\">Shift JIS (Japanese)</option>\n<option value=\"euc-kr\">EUC-KR (Korean)</option>\n<option value=\"ibm866\">CP866 (Russian)</option>\n<option value=\"koi8-r\">KOI8-R (Russian)</option>\n<option value=\"koi8-u\">KOI8-U (Ukrainian)</option>\n<option value=\"macintosh\">Macintosh (x-mac-roman)</option>\n<option value=\"x-mac-cyrillic\">Mac OS Cyrillic (x-mac-cyrillic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-1\">ISO-8859-1 (Latin1/Western European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-2\">ISO-8859-2 (Latin2/Eastern European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-3\">ISO-8859-3 (Latin3/South European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-4\">ISO-8859-4 (Latin4/North European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-5\">ISO-8859-5 (Latin/Cyrillic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-6\">ISO-8859-6 (Latin/Arabic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-7\">ISO-8859-7 (Latin/Greek)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-8\">ISO-8859-8 (Latin/Hebrew)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-8-i\">ISO-8859-8-I (Latin/Hebrew)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-10\">ISO-8859-10 (Latin6/Nordic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-13\">ISO-8859-13 (Latin7/Baltic Rim)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-14\">ISO-8859-14 (Latin8/Celtic)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-15\">ISO-8859-15 (Latin9/Western European)</option>\n<option value=\"iso-8859-16\">ISO-8859-16 (Latin10/South-Eastern European)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-874\">Windows-874 (Thai)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1250\">Windows-1250 (Eastern European)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1251\">Windows-1251 (Cyrillic)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1252\">Windows-1252 (Western European)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1253\">Windows-1253 (Greek)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1254\">Windows-1254 (Turkish)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1255\">Windows-1255 (Hebrew)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1256\">Windows-1256 (Arabic)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1257\">Windows-1257 (Baltic)</option>\n<option value=\"windows-1258\">Windows-1258 (Vietnamese)</option>\n</select></div>\n<div id=\"cdivfilename\" style=\"display:none;padding-top: 8px;\">Output file name: <input class=\"infull\" name=\"cFilename\" type=\"text\"/></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 8px 0px;\">\n<span id=\"spanencode\"><input name=\"e\" onclick=\"return bcEncodeFull();\" type=\"submit\" value=\" Encode\"/></span>\n<span id=\"spandecode\" style=\"display:none;\"><input name=\"d\" onclick=\"return bcDecodeFull();\" type=\"submit\" value=\" Decode\"/></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div id=\"c2outputdesc\"></div>\n<div id=\"c2outputarea\" style=\"display:none;\"><textarea class=\"infulltxarea\" name=\"coutput\" readonly=\"\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</form>\n</div>\n<style>\n#cFileInput::file-selector-button {\n\tbackground-color: #044284;\n\tcolor: white;\n\tpadding: 6px 8px;\n\tborder: none;\n\tborder-radius: 2px;\n\tbox-shadow: 1px 1px 2px #666;\n\tfont-size:16px;\n}\n#cFileInput::file-selector-button:hover {\n\tbackground-color: #0056b3;\n}\n</style>\n<script>\nvar cFileInput = document.calcfull.cFileInput;\nvar cFileContent = \"\";\ncFileInput.addEventListener('change', cHandleFileSelection);\nfunction cHandleFileSelection(cEvent) {\n\tconst cFile = cEvent.target.files[0];\n\tif (cFile) {\n\t\tconst cReader = new FileReader();\n\t\tcReader.onload = (e) => { cFileContent = e.target.result; };\n\t\tcReader.onerror = () => {console.error(\"Unable to read the file.\");};\n\t\tcReader.readAsBinaryString(cFile);\n\t}\n}\nfunction bcCopyOutput2() {\n\tlet bcTxt = document.calcfull.coutput.value + \"\";\n\ttry {\n\t\tnavigator.clipboard.writeText(bcTxt);\n\t} catch (err) {\n\t\tdocument.calcfull.coutput.select();\n\t\tdocument.execCommand('copy');\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\nfunction bcDownloadBin(base64String) {\n\tlet bcDfilename = document.calcfull.cFilename.value + \"\";\n\tif (bcDfilename.length<1) bcDfilename = \"base64-\"+(Date.now()%10000)+\"\";\n\tconst byteCharacters = atob(base64String);\n\tconst byteNumbers = new Array(byteCharacters.length);\n\tfor (let i = 0; i < byteCharacters.length; i++) {byteNumbers[i] = byteCharacters.charCodeAt(i);}\n\tconst byteArray = new Uint8Array(byteNumbers);\n\t//const blob = new Blob([byteArray], { type: \"image/png\" });\n\tconst blob = new Blob([byteArray]);\n\tconst url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n\tconst link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n\tlink.href = url;\n\tlink.download = bcDfilename;\n\tdocument.body.appendChild(link);\n\tlink.click();\n\tdocument.body.removeChild(link);\n\tURL.revokeObjectURL(url);\n\treturn false;\n}\nfunction cOpChange(cocVal){\n\tdocument.getElementById(\"c2outputdesc\").innerHTML = \"\";\n\tdocument.calcfull.coutput.value = \"\";\n\tif (\"en\"==cocVal){\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivfiletype').style.display = \"none\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivchar').style.display = \"none\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivfilename').style.display = \"none\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('spanencode').style.display = \"block\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('spandecode').style.display = \"none\";\n\t}else{\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivfiletype').style.display = \"block\";\n\t\tif (\"txt\"==document.calcfull.cfiletype.value){\n\t\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivchar').style.display = \"block\";\n\t\t}else{\n\t\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivchar').style.display = \"none\";\n\t\t}\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivfilename').style.display = \"block\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('spanencode').style.display = \"none\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('spandecode').style.display = \"block\";\n\t}\n}\nfunction cFileTypeChange(cftcVal){\n\tif (\"txt\"==cftcVal){\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivchar').style.display = \"block\";\n\t}else{\n\t\tdocument.getElementById('cdivchar').style.display = \"none\";\n\t}\n}\nfunction bcEncodeFull(){\n\tlet bceOutputdesc = document.getElementById(\"c2outputdesc\");\n\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = 'processing...';\n\ttry {\n\t\tif ((cFileContent+\"\").length < 1){\n\t\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Please provide a file with content to encode.</font>';\n\t\t}else{\n\t\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"c2outputarea\").style.display = \"block\";\n\t\t\tlet bcEncoder = new TextEncoder();\n\t\t\tdocument.calcfull.coutput.value = btoa(cFileContent);\n\t\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<b>Encoded result:</b> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcCopyOutput2();\"><img src=\"img/copy.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"20\" alt=\"copy\" align=\"absmiddle\">copy</a> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcDownloadTxtFile(document.calcfull.coutput, document.calcfull.cFilename.value);\"><img src=\"img/download.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"download\" align=\"absmiddle\">download</a>';\n\t\t}\n\t} catch (err) {\n\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Sorry, the file cannot be encoded.</font>';\n\t\tdocument.calcfull.coutput.value = \"\";\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\nfunction bcDecodeFull(){\n\tlet bceOutputdesc = document.getElementById(\"c2outputdesc\");\n\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = 'processing...';\n\ttry {\n\t\tif ((cFileContent+\"\").length < 1){\n\t\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Please provide a file with content to decode.</font>';\n\t\t}else{\n\t\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"c2outputarea\").style.display = \"block\";\n\t\t\tif (\"txt\"==document.calcfull.cfiletype.value){\n\t\t\t\tlet bcDecoder = new TextDecoder(document.calcfull.cchar.value + \"\");\n\t\t\t\tdocument.calcfull.coutput.value = bcDecoder.decode(bcB64ToInt8Arr(cFileContent));\n\t\t\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<b>Decoded result:</b> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcCopyOutput2();\"><img src=\"img/copy.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"20\" alt=\"copy\" align=\"absmiddle\">copy</a> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcDownloadTxtFile(document.calcfull.coutput, document.calcfull.cFilename.value);\"><img src=\"img/download.svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\"download\" align=\"absmiddle\">download</a>';\n\t\t\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"c2outputarea\").style.display = \"block\";\n\t\t\t}else{\n\t\t\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"c2outputarea\").style.display = \"none\";\n\t\t\t\tbcDownloadBin(cFileContent);\n\t\t\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<b>Decoded result:</b> <a href=\"#\" onClick=\"return bcDownloadBin(cFileContent);\">download</a>';\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t} catch (err) {\n\t\tbceOutputdesc.innerHTML = '<font color=\"red\">Sorry, the file cannot be Base64-decoded.</font>';\n\t\tdocument.calcfull.coutput.value = \"\";\n\t\tdocument.getElementById(\"c2outputarea\").style.display = \"none\";\n\t}\n\treturn false;\n}\n</script>\n<br/><br/>\n<p>Base64 encoding and decoding is a method used to convert binary data to and from text format. Some computer systems—especially legacy systems—and certain transmission or storage formats are designed to handle text more reliably than raw binary data. Base64 encoding allows binary information, such as images, files, or other data, to be represented using a set of 64 printable ASCII characters, making it suitable for use in these systems and environments.</p>\n<p>The Base64 character set includes uppercase letters A–Z, lowercase letters a–z, digits 0–9, and two additional characters, usually + and /. The symbol = is sometimes used as padding at the end of the encoded output to ensure that the encoded string has the proper length. The following table shows the Base64 characters and their corresponding numeric values based on RFC 4648.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" class=\"cinfoT cinfoTS\">\n<tr><td>0: A</td><td>8: I</td><td>16: Q</td><td>24: Y</td><td>32: g</td><td>40: o</td><td>48: w </td><td>56: 4</td></tr>\n<tr><td>1: B</td><td>9: J</td><td>17: R</td><td>25: Z</td><td>33: h</td><td>41: p</td><td>49: x </td><td>57: 5</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2: C</td><td>10: K</td><td>18: S</td><td>26: a</td><td>34: i</td><td>42: q</td><td>50: y </td><td>58: 6</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3: D</td><td>11: L</td><td>19: T</td><td>27: b</td><td>35: j</td><td>43: r</td><td>51: z </td><td>59: 7</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4: E</td><td>12: M</td><td>20: U</td><td>28: c</td><td>36: k</td><td>44: s</td><td>52: 0</td><td>60: 8</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5: F</td><td>13: N</td><td>21: V</td><td>29: d</td><td>37: l</td><td>45: t</td><td>53: 1</td><td>61: 9</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6: G</td><td>14: O</td><td>22: W</td><td>30: e</td><td>38: m</td><td>46: u</td><td>54: 2</td><td>62: +</td></tr>\n<tr><td>7: H</td><td>15: P</td><td>23: X</td><td>31: f</td><td>39: n</td><td>47: v</td><td>55: 3</td><td>63: /</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Modern computers are byte-based (8 bits per byte), while Base64 encoding represents data using 6-bit values mapped to 64 characters. As a result, Base64-encoded data is typically about 4/3 (≈1.33) times the size of the original data.</p>\n<p>As an example, the simple text 'Dog' can be encoded in Base64 as 'RG9n,' as shown in the table below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" class=\"cinfoT cinfoTS\">\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">Input letter</td><td colspan=\"8\">D</td><td colspan=\"8\">o</td><td colspan=\"8\">g</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">8-bit decimal value</td><td colspan=\"8\">68</td><td colspan=\"8\">111</td><td colspan=\"8\">103</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bits</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">6-bit decimal value</td><td colspan=\"6\">17</td><td colspan=\"6\">6</td><td colspan=\"6\">61</td><td colspan=\"6\">39</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">Encoded Base64 letter</td><td colspan=\"6\">R</td><td colspan=\"6\">G</td><td colspan=\"6\">9</td><td colspan=\"6\">n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>In the example above, the three ASCII characters in 'Dog' have a total of 3 × 8 = 24 bits. This can be divided evenly into four 6-bit blocks. In many cases, there will be 2 or 4 bits remaining at the end. In such situations, one or two '=' padding characters are added to the end of the encoded result to represent the missing bits. For example, 'Do' can be encoded in Base64 as 'RG8=,' as shown below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" class=\"cinfoT cinfoTS\">\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">Input letter</td><td colspan=\"8\">D</td><td colspan=\"8\">o</td><td colspan=\"3\" rowspan=\"2\"> </td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">8-bit decimal value</td><td colspan=\"8\">68</td><td colspan=\"8\">111</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bits</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td style=\"color:red;\">0</td><td style=\"color:red;\">0</td><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"color:red;\">Padding</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">6-bit decimal value</td><td colspan=\"6\">17</td><td colspan=\"6\">6</td><td colspan=\"6\">60</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">Encoded Base64 letter</td><td colspan=\"6\">R</td><td colspan=\"6\">G</td><td colspan=\"6\">8</td><td style=\"color:red;\">=</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Similarly, 'Dogs' can be encoded in Base64 as 'RG9ncw==,' as shown below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" class=\"cinfoT cinfoTS\">\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">Input letter</td><td colspan=\"8\">D</td><td colspan=\"8\">o</td><td colspan=\"8\">g</td><td colspan=\"8\">s</td><td colspan=\"5\" rowspan=\"2\"> </td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">8-bit decimal value</td><td colspan=\"8\">68</td><td colspan=\"8\">111</td><td colspan=\"8\">103</td><td colspan=\"8\">115</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bits</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td style=\"color:red;\">0</td><td style=\"color:red;\">0</td><td style=\"color:red;\">0</td><td style=\"color:red;\">0</td><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"color:red;\">Padding</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">6-bit decimal value</td><td colspan=\"6\">17</td><td colspan=\"6\">6</td><td colspan=\"6\">61</td><td colspan=\"6\">39</td><td colspan=\"6\">28</td><td colspan=\"6\">48</td></tr>\n<tr align=\"center\"><td align=\"left\">Encoded Base64 letter</td><td colspan=\"6\">R</td><td colspan=\"6\">G</td><td colspan=\"6\">9</td><td colspan=\"6\">n</td><td colspan=\"6\">c</td><td colspan=\"6\">w</td><td style=\"color:red;\">==</td></tr>\n</table>\n<br/><p>Base64 encoding and decoding are widely used in data transmission, web development, and file processing. The following are two examples of many uses:</p>\n<p><b>E-mail attachments:</b> Originally, SMTP was designed to transport only 7-bit ASCII characters. Encoding binary data using Base64 allows older SMTP servers to correctly transmit attachments.</p>\n<p><b>Embedding binary data in text files:</b> Text-based formats are widely used in computer systems, especially for transmitting data over the internet. Base64 enables the embedding of binary data in these text files. For example, binary data can be Base64-encoded and included in JSON or XML files. Images or PDF files can also be Base64-encoded and embedded in HTML or CSS. The following is the embeddable HTML for the PNG image of <img align=\"absmiddle\" src=\"/data:image/png;base64,\"/>.</p>\n<div class=\"panel smalltext\" style=\"word-break: break-all;\">&lt;img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /&gt;</div>\n<p>There are numerous online and offline tools, as well as built-in commands in operating systems, to convert data to and from Base64 format. Our tools above provide a convenient way to perform these conversions directly in the browser without sending data across the internet.</p>"}